# Who is asked to review a change here.
#
# One line, every path: with a single maintainer, a per-path table writes the
# same handle on every row and reads as a review boundary that does not exist.
# What this buys is a review request on every pull request from outside,
# including the ones Renovate opens.
#
# The handle must be a user with write access to this repository. GitHub
# silently ignores a rule whose owner it cannot resolve, so a rename turns this
# file off rather than failing it.

